      "id": 1,
      "text": "Marina del Rey got its name when Public Law 87‑402 officially renamed the Playa Del Rey Inlet and Harbor in 1965.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina_del_Rey%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The harbor is North America’s largest man‑made small‑craft marina, offering slips for roughly 5,000 boats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina_del_Rey%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before becoming a marina, the site was an estuary popular with duck hunters and fishermen until the 1965 dedication.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.liveworkplaymdr.com/about-marina-del-rey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Marina del Rey has been a backdrop for films and TV shows, from “Meet the Fockers” to “Modern Family” and “NCIS.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.liveworkplaymdr.com/about-marina-del-rey",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Visitors often spot California sea lions and harbor seals lounging on the docks, while dolphins and whales occasionally drift into deeper waters.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marina_del_Rey%2C_California",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Lloyd Taber‑Marina del Rey Library houses a dedicated nautical collection that serves the local boating community.",
